# Git Standards

- Use Conventional Commits.
- Keep commits atomic and logically scoped.
- Use the repository's configured Git author identity.
- Never append `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: AI`, or other AI co-author trailers.
- Do not add AI attribution footers to PR descriptions.
- Do not claim AI-assisted code was developed entirely by a human.
- Respect mandatory repository and organization policies.
- Never change Git author identity without permission.
- Never backdate commits to fabricate development activity.
- Never amend or force-push without explicit approval.
- Verify build and relevant tests before committing.
- Do not create PRs automatically.
